---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice, Jjodel application | Jjodel"
  description="How the Jjodel application at app.jjodel.io handles the personal data of its users."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Notice for the Jjodel application</h1>
      <p class="muted">
        Last updated: 18 October 2026. This notice covers app.jjodel.io and is
        given under Articles 13 and 14 of the EU General Data Protection
        Regulation (GDPR). The website jjodel.io has its own short{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Data controller</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The controller is the University of L'Aquila (Università degli Studi
        dell'Aquila), Italy. For questions about this notice or your data,
        write to <a href="mailto:info@jjodel.io">info@jjodel.io</a>. You can
        also contact the University's Data Protection Officer, whose details
        are published on{' '}
        <a href="https://www.univaq.it" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          www.univaq.it ↗
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        When you register: first name, last name, nickname, affiliation,
        country, email address and password (stored only in hashed form).
        While you use the application: the projects you save (metamodels,
        models, viewpoints, transformations and related content) and the
        technical data that any web service records, such as IP address,
        request times and error logs.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        We use your data to create and run your account, store your projects,
        let you share them with other users, send you the emails the service
        needs (account activation and password reset) and keep the service
        secure. The legal basis is the provision of the service you request
        (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR). We also use the affiliation and country of
        registered users, in aggregate form only, to report how Jjodel is used
        in research and teaching, as part of the University's institutional
        tasks (Art. 6(1)(e) GDPR). We do not send newsletters or marketing
        emails, and we do not sell or rent your data.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Who can see your data</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Other users see your name and nickname only when you share a project
        with them or collaborate with them; your email address is not shown.
        The application is hosted on Microsoft Azure in Italy: Microsoft acts
        as a processor on behalf of the University. Members of the Jjodel team
        at the University can access data when needed to operate and support
        the service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">AI features</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The Jjodie assistant uses an API key that you enter for a provider of
        your choice. The key is kept in your browser's local storage. When you
        use the assistant, the content of your requests is sent to that
        provider, which may be located outside the European Union and handles
        it under its own privacy policy. Requests to Anthropic and Google
        Gemini pass through a relay run by the Jjodel team on Cloudflare
        Workers, used only to forward them. If you do not enter a key, no
        content is sent to any AI provider.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Browser storage</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The application stores your session and preferences in your browser
        (local storage). It does not use advertising or tracking cookies and
        does not use analytics services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Account data and projects are kept for as long as your account
        exists. There is currently no automatic deletion of inactive accounts:
        when you ask us to delete your account, we delete your personal data
        and your projects, except where the law requires us to keep them.
        Technical logs are kept for a limited period for security purposes.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        You can ask to access, correct or delete your data, to restrict or
        object to its processing, and to receive your data in a portable
        format, by writing to{' '}
        <a href="mailto:info@jjodel.io">info@jjodel.io</a>. You also have the
        right to lodge a complaint with the Italian data protection authority,
        the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Garante per la protezione dei dati personali ↗
        </a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
